From 11fce1b85535a560c950ab8029a893ad528d6728 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:07:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/21] Bound TTM-to-fiscal-year agreement by the rounding of
 the reported figures

The fixed 0.5% tolerance had no basis and let a 55 million gap through on
a 76 billion total. A TTM window that is exactly a fiscal year may now
differ from that year's reported value only by what the rounding of the
five figures can explain: half the last stated unit of each, with a zero
taking the finest precision of the others. Of the 29 such windows in the
current imports, 24 agree within rounding and 5 are withheld as conflicts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CfTpoii6QDStyTPdotmEdY
